Chunked gated-delta-net prefill on CDNA (+12% prefill on gfx90a)

Self-contained: bundles upstream PR #26001 (BLSharda, unmerged as of
2026-08-10, pinned at 1e1885f3d) together with the four fixes needed to make
its ggml_cuda_mma path actually run on AMD CDNA. Applies to a bare
67b9b0e checkout, so the Dockerfile can apply it in the normal loop -- same
approach as patches/04, which bundles the upstream SSD kernels with our CDNA
enablement.

The four fixes, each of which masked the next:

  1. cgdr_precompute_qk_wmma_kernel launched a 32-thread block, but AMD MFMA
     tiles span a full 64-lane wavefront (mma.cuh: ne = I*J/64), so half the
     16x16 accumulator's lanes did not exist. Load/writeback loops likewise
     assumed 32 lanes owned the whole tile.
  2. __launch_bounds__(32, 8) is a hard ceiling, so the 64-thread launch
     failed outright. Now ggml_cuda_get_physical_warp_size(), as mmid.cu does.
  3. Plain load_ldmatrix has no AMD_MFMA branch in mma.cuh (TURING and
     AMD_WMMA only, then NO_DEVICE_CODE, which traps). The three plain call
     sites use load_generic, defined via the same get_i/get_j.
     load_ldmatrix_trans is untouched -- it does have an MFMA branch.
  4. The 16x16 f32 accumulator fragment is DATA_LAYOUT_J_MAJOR on CDNA/RDNA4,
     but the kernel declared the default I_MAJOR. mma.cuh's J_MAJOR tile is a
     wrapper that swaps get_i/get_j, so every lane wrote its accumulator
     elements to transposed coordinates and the tile was scattered. This was
     the real defect (ERR 1.868 vs a 2e-7 threshold).

Dispatch widened to admit CDNA. NVIDIA conditions unchanged throughout.

Verified on 2x MI210 (gfx90a), ROCm 7.14, stacked on patches 04-12:
  test-backend-ops: GATED_DELTA_NET 50/51, SSM_SCAN 7/7, SSM_CONV 45/45,
                    MUL_MAT 1134/1134, MUL_MAT_ID 790/790
  llama-bench Qwen3.6-40B IQ4_NL: pp2048 606->678 (+11.8%)
                                  pp8192 911->1021 (+12.1%)
  temperature 0, 376-token prompt: byte-identical output vs recurrent

Known: n_seq_tokens=2048 misses at NMSE ~3e-7 against a 2e-7 threshold -- a
precision margin at the most-accumulated shape (128 chunks at CS=16), not a
correctness failure. Reported upstream rather than relaxing the bound.

Caveat: this pins an unmerged PR. If #26001 is force-pushed or merges, this
patch must be re-cut against master (or dropped, if the fixes land with it).

